      "created_at": "2026-03-14T17:10:39Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-14T17:10:39Z",
      "body": "@pi0 This is labeled v1. In v2, the `EventStream` class handles cleanup properly:\n\n- Constructor auto-registers `res.once(\"close\", () => this.close())` for Node.js (via `autoclose` option, enabled by default)\n- `close()` has a `_disposed` guard preventing double-close\n- All write methods check `_writerIsClosed` before writing\n\nCan this be closed as resolved in v2?",
